{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A fool</b> — on the day he walks among men, then his anger is known, that he grows angry with them." "<b>And covereth shame</b> — that the fool speaks against him and he conceals it, he is wise; as in: 'Answer not a fool.' Another interpretation: one who puts on shame has no garment, for he is naked even though he is in Sharon."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:22.594990178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}